<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">Numerical Solution</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L107" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Since we're dealing with a Partial Differential Equation with first-order time derivatives and second-order space derivatives, a reasonable approach to try to solve this problem numerically is the Crank-Nicholson Method.


<Font encoding="UTF-8">We start by approximating the derivatives appearig in the Schr\303\266dinger equation. With that purpose,  and because we're dealing with a linear differential equation, we make use of the &quot;GenerateStencil&quot; proceedure learned in class</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">(a)</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L32" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">restart;
with(PDEtools):
with(plots):
with(LinearAlgebra):
with(Statistics):</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L584" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font encoding="UTF-8">We first write the Schr\303\266dinger equation for an arbitrary time independent potenntial.</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L31" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Sch:= I*hbar*diff(psi(x,y,t),t)=-hbar^2/(2*m)*(diff(psi(x,y,t),x,x)+diff(psi(x,y,t),y,y)+V(x,y)*psi(x,y,t));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L33" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L585" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now we define the &quot;GenerateStencil&quot; proceedure covered in class.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L34" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">GenerateStencil := proc(F, N, {orientation := center, stepsize := h, showorder := true, showerror := false})
    local vars, f, ii, Degree, stencil, Error, unknowns, Indets, ans, Phi, r, n, phi, i;

    Phi := convert(F, D);
    vars := op(Phi);
    n := PDEtools[difforder](Phi);
    f := op(1, op(0, Phi));
    if (nops([vars])&lt;&gt;1) then:
        r := op(1, op(0, op(0, Phi)));
    else:
        r := 1;
    fi:
    phi := f(vars);
    if (orientation = center) then:
        if (type(N, odd)) then:
            ii := [seq(i, i = -(N-1)/2..(N-1)/2)];
        else:
            ii := [seq(i, i = -(N-1)..(N-1), 2)];
        fi;
    elif (orientation = left) then:
        ii := [seq(i, i = -N+1..0)]:
    elif (orientation = right) then:
        ii := [seq(i, i = 0..N-1)]:
    fi;
    stencil := add(a[ii[i]]*subsop(r = op(r, phi)+ii[i]*stepsize, phi), i = 1..N);
    Error := D[r$n](f)(vars)-stencil;
    Error := convert(series(Error, stepsize, N), polynom);
    unknowns := {seq(a[ii[i]], i = 1..N)};
    Indets := indets(Error) minus {vars} minus unknowns minus {stepsize};
    Error := collect(Error, Indets, 'distributed');
    ans := solve({coeffs(Error, Indets)}, unknowns);
    if (ans = NULL) then:
        print(`Failure: try increasing the number of points in the stencil`);
        return NULL;
    fi:
    stencil := subs(ans, stencil);
    Error := convert(series(`leadterm`(D[r$n](f)(vars)-stencil), stepsize, N+20), polynom);
    Degree := degree(Error, stepsize);
    if (showorder) then:
        print(cat(`This stencil is of order `, Degree));
    fi:
    if (showerror) then:
        print(cat(`This leading order term in the error is `, Error));
    fi:
        convert(D[r$n](f)(vars) = stencil, diff);
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L35" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L586" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Next, we Approximate the first-order time derivative appearing in the equation by a 1st order <Font bold="true">Forward</Font> approximation and a first-order <Font bold="true">Backward</Font> approximation. Meanwhile, the second order space derivatives are approximated by a 2nd-order centered approximation.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L36" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">forward_time := GenerateStencil(diff(psi(x,y,t), t), 2, orientation = right, stepsize = s);
backward_time := GenerateStencil(diff(psi(x,y,t), t), 2, orientation = left, stepsize = s);
centered_spacex := GenerateStencil(diff(psi(x,y,t), x, x), 3, orientation = center, stepsize = h);
centered_spacey := GenerateStencil(diff(psi(x,y,t), y,y ), 3, orientation = center, stepsize = r);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbWlHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JVE7VGhpc35zdGVuY2lsfmlzfm9mfm9yZGVyfjFGJy8lJ2l0YWxpY0dRJXRydWVGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1EnaXRhbGljRic=">STtUaGlzfnN0ZW5jaWx+aXN+b2Z+b3JkZXJ+MUc2Ig==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SS1mb3J3YXJkX3RpbWVHRigvLUklZGlmZkdGJjYkLUkkcHNpR0YoNiVJInhHRihJInlHRihJInRHRihGNywmKiZJInNHRighIiJGMiIiIkY7KiZGOkY7LUYzNiVGNUY2LCZGN0Y8RjpGPEY8Rjw3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbWlHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JVE7VGhpc35zdGVuY2lsfmlzfm9mfm9yZGVyfjFGJy8lJ2l0YWxpY0dRJXRydWVGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1EnaXRhbGljRic=">STtUaGlzfnN0ZW5jaWx+aXN+b2Z+b3JkZXJ+MUc2Ig==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SS5iYWNrd2FyZF90aW1lR0YoLy1JJWRpZmZHRiY2JC1JJHBzaUdGKDYlSSJ4R0YoSSJ5R0YoSSJ0R0YoRjcsJiomSSJzR0YoISIiLUYzNiVGNUY2LCZGNyIiIkY6RjtGP0Y7KiZGOkY7RjJGP0Y/NyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbWlHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JVE7VGhpc35zdGVuY2lsfmlzfm9mfm9yZGVyfjJGJy8lJ2l0YWxpY0dRJXRydWVGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1EnaXRhbGljRic=">STtUaGlzfnN0ZW5jaWx+aXN+b2Z+b3JkZXJ+Mkc2Ig==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbWlHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JVE7VGhpc35zdGVuY2lsfmlzfm9mfm9yZGVyfjJGJy8lJ2l0YWxpY0dRJXRydWVGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1EnaXRhbGljRic=">STtUaGlzfnN0ZW5jaWx+aXN+b2Z+b3JkZXJ+Mkc2Ig==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L587" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font encoding="UTF-8">We use this approximations to generate a Forward-in-Time-Centered-in-Space  (FTCS) and a Backward-in-Time-Centered-in-Space (BTCS) stencils for the Schr\303\266dinger Equation</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L37" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">FTCS_stencil := subs(forward_time, centered_spacex, centered_spacey, Sch);
BTCS_stencil := subs(backward_time, centered_spacex, centered_spacey, Sch):
BTCS_stencil := subs(t = t+s, BTCS_stencil);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L199" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L200" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">FTCS_stencil := expand(isolate(FTCS_stencil, psi(x,y,t+s)));
BTCS_stencil := expand(isolate(BTCS_stencil, psi(x,y,t))):
BTCS_stencil := rhs(BTCS_stencil) = lhs(BTCS_stencil);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L588" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Then, a Crank-Nicholson stencil for this equation is generated by averaging the FTCS and BTCS stencils, just like with the Trapezoidal method</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L201" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">CN_stencil := (FTCS_stencil+BTCS_stencil)/2;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L202" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Subs := [seq(seq(seq(psi(x+jj*h,y+kk*r, t+ii*s) = psi[j+jj, k+kk, i+ii],kk=-1..1), jj = -1..1), ii = 0..1)]:
CN_general := subs(Subs,V(x,y)=V[j][k], CN_stencil);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L215" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L589" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font encoding="UTF-8">It should be emphasized that, up until this point, no reference to the particular form of the potential for this problem has been made. This means that the CN stencil generated at the previous equations is applicable to solve Schr\303\266dinger's equation numerically for an arbitrary potential V(x,y).
</Font>
The generated stencil relates the values of the wave function at particular time step i, to its values at the next time step i+1. This wave function has value ate every point of a finite Two-Dimensional Grid on the XY Plane, where the coordinates fo the points are labeled by j,k. Evolving the wave function in time means to find the values of the wave function at all the points of the grid for the next time step.

<Font encoding="UTF-8">Let's work now with a specific case: Let's set up a 2x2 space grid, and try to evolve the system in 10 time steps, up to some final time \317\204=1 (We will work on units where \342\204\217=1, and we will take the mass of the particle to be </Font><Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>). For these choices of the parameters, we evaluate the CN Stencil for all the points in the grid, and make use of the Boundary conditions.
</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">From the stencil, we can also see that we need to evaluate the potential at every point of the space grid. It is then at this stage, where we introduce the form of our potential, and evaluate it at every point of the grid

</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L203" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">M := 2;
N:= 2;
t:=10;
L:=10;
tau:=1;
A:=sqrt(2/evalf(Pi));
f:=(x,y)-&gt;A*exp(-((x+5)^2+(y)^2))*exp(I*x); #Set up the initial condition
U:=(x,y)-&gt;piecewise(x&gt;0,5,x&lt;0,0); #Define the potential
X := a -&gt; -L+a*2*L/(M+1);
Y := b -&gt; -L+b*2*L/(N+1);
T := c -&gt; tau*c/t;
s := evalf(T(1)-T(0)); #Time step
h := evalf(X(1)-X(0)); #X Spacestep
r := evalf(Y(1)-Y(0)); #Y Spacestep
m:=hbar^2/2;
hbar:=1;

#Generate the Spatial Grid
XX := Vector([seq(X(a), a = 1..M)], datatype = float):
YY := Vector([seq(Y(b), b = 1..N)], datatype = float):

V:=[seq([seq(U(X(a),Y(b)),b=1..N)],a=1..M)]: #Initialize values of the Potential at the points of the grid

psi_past:=Vector([seq(seq([evalf(f(XX[a],YY[b]))],b=1..N),a=1..M)]): #Initial Conditions

#Boundary Conditions
psi[0,k,i+1] := 0;    
psi[M+1,k,i+1] := 0;
psi[0,k,i] := 0;
psi[M+1,k,i] := 0;
psi[j,0,i+1] := 0;
psi[j,N+1,i+1] := 0;
psi[j,0,i] := 0;
psi[j,N+1,i] := 0;
for jj from 1 to M do:  #Here we generate the system of equations
    for kk from 1 to N do:
        sys[jj][kk] := eval(eval(CN_general, k = kk),j=jj);
        sys[jj][kk]:=subs(psi[0,kk,i+1]=0,psi[M+1,kk,i+1]= 0,psi[0,kk,i]=0,psi[M+1,kk,i]=0,psi[jj,0,i+1]=0,psi[jj,N+1,i+1]=0,psi[jj,0,i]=0,psi[j,N+1,i]=0,sys[jj][kk]);
    od;
od;
</Text-field>
